00:12:51,726 --> 00:12:54,020
我根本不记得她是我们的保姆
and, uh, I didn't even remember she was our babysitter.

348
00:12:54,820 --> 00:12:55,340
真的吗
Really?

349
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:57,340
是啊  然后她约我出去
Yeah. Then she asked me out,

350
00:12:57,340 --> 00:12:58,880
你也知道  约我的不多
and you know, I don't get a lot of offers,

351
00:12:58,900 --> 00:13:00,040
我就想  "管他的"
so I thought, "What the heck?"

352
00:13:00,640 --> 00:13:02,100
我猜也是
Sure. That's what I figured.

353
00:13:02,140 --> 00:13:04,600
但我很高兴你过得愉快
But, uh, I'm just glad you're having fun.

354
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:06,200
我最好去把我这瓶子
Well, I better go fill this thing up

355
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:08,280
装满杰昂贵的威士忌了
with some of Jay's expensive Scotch.

356
00:13:09,178 --> 00:13:10,185
其实  门似乎锁上了
Oh, actually, I think the door's locked.

357
00:13:11,533 --> 00:13:12,297
没有  好得很
Oh, no, it's fine.

358
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:16,100
弗兰克  非常抱歉水管喷到你了
Well, Frank, I'm really sorry about that hose thing.

359
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:17,507
没什么
Oh, no hard feelings.

360
00:13:17,800 --> 00:13:19,320
我衣服也该洗洗了
Shirt needed freshening anyway.

361
00:13:19,718 --> 00:13:20,361
反正打从
I haven't washed it

362
00:13:20,421 --> 00:13:22,009
上次我们停车下来跟火轮海拍照就没洗了
since we stopped to take pictures at Smokey-Top,

363
00:13:23,160 --> 00:13:26,520
火轮海是犹他州历时最长的轮胎弃置场大火
Utah's longest, continuously burning tire fire.

364
00:13:28,520 --> 00:13:31,960
我猜你也听到了  我完全没什么好担心
As I guess you heard, I had no reason to be worried.

365
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:34,160
他本来都没意识到洛林曾是我的保姆
He didn't even notice when Lorraine was my babysitter.

366
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:35,720
而且他们也不是太认真在谈恋爱
Plus, they're not even that serious.

367
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:37,580
我摸到了他口袋里有戒指盒
I felt a ring box in his pocket.

368
00:13:37,580 --> 00:13:38,620
什么  不可能
What? No way.

369
00:13:39,080 --> 00:13:39,160
真的
Yep.

370
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:41,160
世上没有别的东西是那个形状了
There's only one thing shaped like that.

371
00:13:41,160 --> 00:13:43,240
才没有  那形状的东西多了
No, there isn't. There's a million things --

372
00:13:43,240 --> 00:13:45,140
魔方  针线包
Rubik's Cube, sewing kit,

373
00:13:45,160 --> 00:13:46,535
火轮海的纪念品轮胎钥匙圈
souvenir tire keychain from Smokey-Top.

374
00:13:47,180 --> 00:13:48,860
我都想不出有什么东西不是那形状了
I can't think of anything that's not shaped like that.

375
00:13:48,860 --> 00:13:50,580
我们就先假设一下我感觉对了
Let's assume for a moment that I am right

376
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:51,740
那真的是戒指盒
and that was a ring box.

377
00:13:51,740 --> 00:13:53,020
我觉得挺值得探讨
Maybe it's worth exploring

378
00:13:53,020 --> 00:13:54,400
为什么你爸爸续弦
why the idea of your dad remarrying

379
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:55,600
会让你这么惴惴不安
is setting you off like this.

380
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:56,680
或许也很值得探讨
Maybe it's worth exploring

381
00:13:56,791 --> 00:13:58,707
为什么你这么享受把人搞崩溃
why you find so much joy in tearing people down.

382
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:00,120
在早年
In previous generations,

383
00:14:00,140 --> 00:14:01,718
人们可是会说你们这种人是女巫
they accused people like that of being witches

384
00:14:01,738 --> 00:14:03,012
朝你们泼水  如果尖叫就真是女巫
and threw water at them to see if they screamed.

385
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:03,700
好棒棒
Great.

386
00:14:04,588 --> 00:14:05,571
女巫
Witch.

387
00:14:09,360 --> 00:14:10,770
我猜您就是普里契特先生吧
Ah, Mr. Pritchett, I presume.

388
00:14:11,113 --> 00:14:12,281
你好  谢谢你辛苦跑这一趟
Hi. Thank you so much for coming.

389
00:14:12,321 --> 00:14:13,973
我不太确定我有没有听对你名字
I'm not sure I caught your name.

390
00:14:13,983 --> 00:14:15,738
-基夫斯·班克斯  -太好了
- Keifth Banks. - Yes.

391
00:14:15,748 --> 00:14:16,010
随时为您...
At your --

392
00:14:16,616 --> 00:14:17,525
米奇尔  抱歉打断你了
Mitchell, sorry to interrupt.

393
00:14:17,545 --> 00:14:19,200
我不知道你在跟个普通工人聊天
I didn't know you were with a common worker.

394
00:14:19,820 --> 00:14:21,460
万万没想到
Can it be?

395
00:14:22,620 --> 00:14:23,740
卡梅隆·塔克
Cameron Tucker.

396
00:14:24,420 --> 00:14:26,640
是的  不好意思  您是...
Yes. I'm sorry. You are...?

397
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:28,604
基夫斯
Keifth.

398
00:14:28,630 --> 00:14:29,454
基夫斯  我好像不记得有认识...
Keifth. I-I don't believe I know --

399
00:14:30,218 --> 00:14:31,404
不对  小卡  你不是跟我说过
No, C-Cam, didn't you tell me

400
00:14:31,424 --> 00:14:32,952
你曾跟一个叫基夫斯的人在一起过吗
you once dated someone named Keifth?

401
00:14:34,379 --> 00:14:35,395
对啊  基夫斯
Oh, yes. Keifth.

402
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:37,960
你当年是做什么的来著
What was it you did again?

403
00:14:38,060 --> 00:14:40,940
我记得你戴著白手套  然后很多肢体动作
I remember you wore white gloves and -- and gestured a lot.

404
00:14:41,064 --> 00:14:41,406
地铁站的默剧演出者吗
Subway mime?

405
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:44,000
我是马戏团的领导
I commanded a circus.

406
00:14:44,560 --> 00:14:46,420
是的  现在我想起来了
Yes. Now I remember.

407
00:14:46,420 --> 00:14:47,260
你还好吗
How have you been?

408
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:48,900
你现在干起送猪到府的行当了吗
I see you're in pig delivery now?

409
00:14:48,960 --> 00:14:49,640
我是一位礼宾人员
I'm a concierge.

410
00:14:50,480 --> 00:14:52,900
马戏团的行当这年头越来越艰难
The circus business has gotten rather difficult.

411
00:14:52,900 --> 00:14:54,520
现在的人没有那种耐心
People today, they don't have the patience

412
00:14:54,520 --> 00:14:57,040
去欣赏早年那种更优雅的演出了
for the more elegant pleasures of yesteryear --

413
00:14:57,040 --> 00:14:59,240
比如看人把头放进狮子嘴里
men putting their heads into lion's mouths,

414
00:14:59,240 --> 00:15:01,480
可怜的侏儒被从大炮里射出
unfortunate little people being shot from cannons.

415
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:04,400
真不敢相信  你们会在这种情况下重逢
I can't believe you-- you're meeting up again like this.

416
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:06,200
你们之间肯定有很多话想聊
You must have so much to catch up on

417
00:15:06,281 --> 00:15:07,950
或很多事想处理吧
or -- or -- or work through.

418
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:09,913
我相信基夫斯比较想
Oh, well, I'm sure Keifth would rather

419
00:15:09,973 --> 00:15:12,329
把东西送到之后就人间蒸发吧
just make the delivery and disappear.

420
00:15:12,380 --> 00:15:13,700
就从这个开始处理
Start there.

421
00:15:13,700 --> 00:15:14,680
说说手里的这问题
To the matter at hand.

422
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:17,420
要大换烤猪是比较困难的
The swap will be difficult.

423
00:15:17,940 --> 00:15:20,620
幸好我对误导观众目光焦点颇有经验
Fortunately, I have had a bit of experience with misdirects --

424
00:15:20,620 --> 00:15:23,100
只需要叫观众集中注意看著舞台中央
just tell the audience to keep your eyes on the center ring!

425
00:15:23,940 --> 00:15:25,460
他们就不会发现舞台上方的空中飞人
They won't even notice the trapeze act

426
00:15:25,460 --> 00:15:28,060
正在艰难地度过食物中毒反应较大的阶段
suffering through the more vivid stages of food poisoning.

427
00:15:28,060 --> 00:15:29,500
真事  我当时也在场
That happened. I was there.

428
00:15:29,500 --> 00:15:34,800
首先  我放出一只活孔雀
First, I will release a live peacock --

429
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:37,340
来自东方的异国珍兽  进后院
an exotic beauty of the Orient -- into the yard.

430
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:38,820
太魔幻
Magical.

431
00:15:38,820 --> 00:15:42,500
然后我需要有能把它吸引进屋的东西
Then, I will need something to lure him inside

432
00:15:42,500 --> 00:15:43,980
好吸引所有人的注意力
to draw the family's attention.

433
00:15:44,010 --> 00:15:46,140
你们有西班牙安达卢西亚的榛果吗
Do you happen to have any Andalusian filberts?

434
00:15:46,150 --> 00:15:47,745
没有
No.

435
00:15:47,755 --> 00:15:48,300
那就用起司小饼干吧
Then Cheez-Its will do.

436
00:15:48,880 --> 00:15:50,360
普通人在这时候都会呆住
Naturally, everyone will be transfixed.

437
00:15:50,360 --> 00:15:52,640
这时趁他们不注意  我们就把猪给换了
And while they're distracted, we will swap out the pigs,

438
00:15:52,640 --> 00:15:55,980
晚餐就起死回生  表演就能继续
the dinner will be saved, and the show will go on.

439
00:15:55,980 --> 00:15:57,600
让我先偷看一眼后院
Just let me sneak a peek at the backyard.

440
00:16:00,520 --> 00:16:01,000
再见啦
Goodbye.

441
00:16:02,560 --> 00:16:03,520
乔
Hey, Joe,

442
00:16:03,520 --> 00:16:07,080
什么东西有两头四脚还会飞
what has two heads, four legs, and can fly?

443
00:16:07,110 --> 00:16:08,462
不知道
I don't know.

444
00:16:08,673 --> 00:16:10,204
我们
Us. Aah!

445
00:16:10,626 --> 00:16:12,200
这样很危险
This is dangerous!

446
00:16:12,210 --> 00:16:14,470
玩心跳才知道自己还活著啊
That's how you know we're alive!

447
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:16,214
就像我在婚礼致辞时说的
It's like I said in my wedding toast --

448
00:16:16,254 --> 00:16:17,666
你的新娘天不怕地不怕
that bride of yours is fearless.

449
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:19,440
对啊
Yeah.

450
00:16:19,440 --> 00:16:22,420
而奇怪的是  今天早先我们去了游乐园
Funny thing is, we went to an amusement park earlier today

451
00:16:22,420 --> 00:16:25,060
她却不敢去坐其中一个设施
and she was too scared to get on this one ride.

452
00:16:26,240 --> 00:16:28,180
又或者她假装不敢
Or she pretended to be

453
00:16:28,180 --> 00:16:30,780
这样我就不用承认自己有多怕坐那个了
so that I wouldn't have to admit how scared I was.

454
00:16:32,300 --> 00:16:34,020
我有个感觉  她不是今天
I have a hunch that she's not the only one

455
00:16:34,020 --> 00:16:36,320
唯一一个想保护我感受的人
who's trying to protect my feelings today.

456
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:38,160
儿啊  你讲话有点含糊不清啊
You seem to be rambling, son.

457
00:16:40,180 --> 00:16:41,760
你早先跟克莱尔拥抱时
When you hugged Claire earlier,

458
00:16:41,760 --> 00:16:43,560
她摸到你口袋里有戒指盒状物
she felt a ring box in your pocket.

459
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:46,180
什么  那才不是戒指盒
What? That wasn't a ring box.

460
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:49,500
那是...  我现在在哪里  我老糊涂了
It was...where am I? I'm so old and confused.

461
00:16:49,585 --> 00:16:50,552
别演了
Stop.

462
00:16:50,562 --> 00:16:51,930
我不会否认看到你跟洛林在一起
I'm not gonna say seeing you with Lorraine

463
00:16:51,951 --> 00:16:53,410
没有任何别扭的感觉
wasn't a little bit weird for me.

464
00:16:53,420 --> 00:16:55,112
的确是很疯狂的一件事啦
It was a crazy idea.

465
00:16:55,280 --> 00:16:56,340
我要说的不是这个
That's not what I'm trying to say.

466
00:16:56,471 --> 00:16:58,284
那头猪应该烤熟了吧
That pig's got to be ready, doesn't it?

467
00:16:58,294 --> 00:16:58,858
爸  别这样
Dad, please.

468
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:01,760
儿啊  我们能不这样吗
Son, can we please not do this?

469
00:17:02,220 --> 00:17:02,660
好吧
Fine.

470
00:17:03,460 --> 00:17:04,320
咚咚咚
Knock, knock.

471
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:06,020
这还比较像话
That's more like it.

472
00:17:06,020 --> 00:17:06,820
是谁在敲门啊
Who's there?

473
00:17:06,820 --> 00:17:08,140
-你儿子  -哪位你儿子
- Your son. - Your son, who?

474
00:17:08,140 --> 00:17:10,280
你那位不想你因为他而放弃
Your son who'd hate to think you threw away

475
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:12,360
自己幸福的机会来保护他感受的儿子
a shot at happiness just to protect his feelings.

476
00:17:15,640 --> 00:17:17,600
给你  都在这  从我手里拿走它吧
Here it is. All here. Just take it from me.

477
00:17:17,600 --> 00:17:18,640
这是我这辈子压力最大的一次
That's the most stress I've ever felt,

478
00:17:18,849 --> 00:17:19,596
我可是曾在地底待过两周
and I spent two weeks underground

479
00:17:19,656 --> 00:17:20,725
来做孤独有关的研究呢
as part of an isolation study.

480
00:17:21,220 --> 00:17:21,620
好啦
Okay.

481
00:17:21,620 --> 00:17:23,700
我们现在应该能把这弄完啦
So, I guess now we can finish this.

482
00:17:24,269 --> 00:17:25,880
米奇  米奇  过来帮我们填完这个
Ay, Mitch. Mitch, come. Help us finish.

483
00:17:26,360 --> 00:17:28,805
好的  好的  我们用快问快答来填完这些表
Okay. Okay. We got to lightning round these forms.

484
00:17:28,845 --> 00:17:30,330
你们俩都想得太多了
You guys are overthinking this.

485
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:32,019
其实答案早就在每个人心里了
Everybody knows in their heart what they want.

486
00:17:32,040 --> 00:17:33,960
大家只是都不好意思做出那决定
They just feel bad about making the decision.

487
00:17:33,980 --> 00:17:36,394
那开始吧  你要选谁做你的遗嘱执行人  请作答
So, who will be the executor of your estate? Go.

488
00:17:36,617 --> 00:17:37,782
-你  -好的
- You. - Aww. Okay.

489
00:17:38,540 --> 00:17:40,230
你有什么想要捐给慈善机构的吗
Um, do you want to leave anything to charity?

490
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:40,940
有
Yes.

491
00:17:40,940 --> 00:17:44,500
一成财产捐给我们去世时最拉风的慈善项目
10% to whatever is sexy at the time we die --

492
00:17:44,637 --> 00:17:46,794
比如像孤儿什么的吧
like, um, orphans or whatever.

493
00:17:46,840 --> 00:17:48,100
好的  好的  下一题那斯黛拉呢
Okay, okay, yeah. And what about Stella?

494
00:17:48,100 --> 00:17:48,840
跟曼尼一人一半
Same as Manny.

495
00:17:49,320 --> 00:17:51,540
不是  他是在问你斯黛拉该由谁来照顾
No, he's asking who's gonna take care of her,

496
00:17:52,065 --> 00:17:53,660
不是问你打算留多少钱给一个杀人凶手
not how much money you're gonna leave to a murderer.

497
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:55,260
没证据证明她是啊
No proof of that.

498
00:17:55,380 --> 00:17:56,480
好吧  感觉那事值得另外谈过
Okay, this seems like a whole sidebar,

499
00:17:56,520 --> 00:17:58,040
我们一会再绕回来讨论这个吧
so we're gonna circle back to that.

500
00:17:58,187 --> 00:18:00,080
下一个  你想要谁来做乔的法定监护人
Um, who do you want as Joe's legal guardian?

501
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:02,460
别  别去想  按直觉回答一个  好吗
No, no, don't think. Just answer, okay?

502
00:18:02,460 --> 00:18:03,860
如果万一你们两个都遭遇了不幸
If something happens to both of you,

503
00:18:03,990 --> 00:18:05,140
你最想要谁来照顾乔
who do you want to take care of Joe?

504
00:18:07,220 --> 00:18:08,100
我啊  这还用说
Me, obviously.

505
00:18:09,092 --> 00:18:10,783
曼尼  你还太小了
Ay, Manny, you're too young.

506
00:18:10,900 --> 00:18:13,380
而且不久之后你马上就要开始自己新的生活了
Besides, you're about to start your new life soon.

507
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:14,856
是啊  你应该致力出去播种
Yeah, you should be out sowing your oats

508
00:18:14,937 --> 00:18:16,029
或者致力织布吧
or just sewing.

509
00:18:16,090 --> 00:18:17,050
反正你正好喜欢这个
That's something you like.

510
00:18:17,060 --> 00:18:18,573
我不觉得这有什么大问题
I don't see what the big deal is.

511
00:18:18,660 --> 00:18:21,920
我会雇个保姆  卖了房子  换到小点的公寓里
I'd hire a nanny, sell the house, downsize to a condo.

512
00:18:21,940 --> 00:18:24,652
我在考虑正要蓬勃发展的艺术街区的复式楼
I'm thinking maybe a loft in an up-and-coming arts district.

513
00:18:24,860 --> 00:18:27,180
的确  这些事可能会延迟我大学毕业的时间
Sure, it'll take me a bit longer to finish college,

514
00:18:27,180 --> 00:18:29,100
但反正大学也是生命里最好的一段时光  不是吗
but aren't those the best years of life, anyway?

515
00:18:29,840 --> 00:18:31,500
但最重要的是  他是我的弟弟
The main thing is, he's my brother.

516
00:18:31,540 --> 00:18:33,220
我不会答应让除了我之外的人来把他养大
I'm not letting anybody else raise him.

517
00:18:33,764 --> 00:18:36,280
曼尼  你太贴心了
